**Solution 1:** Sorts sets by median, computes T = N-K extras, distributes them per-set via round-robin (ji[i] extras → ai=ceil(ji/2) above, bi=floor(ji/2) below), assigns below values to smallest-c sets and above values to largest-c sets.

**Solution 2:** Sorts sets by median (ascending), computes K_extra (sets with one unpaired above) and pairs = (T-K_extra)/2, distributes pairs evenly (base_p + remainder), assigns below from smallest-c sets and above from smallest-c sets (for flexibility).

